{"id": "EUVD-2026-81842", "enisaUuid": "a95173f1-a589-3301-9705-f75d62278b4f", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\niio: light: gp2ap002: Fix unbalanced runtime PM on repeated event writes\n\nThe IIO core does not filter duplicate writes to the event enable\nattribute, so writing the same value twice invokes\nwrite_event_config() twice. Enabling twice leaks a runtime PM\nreference, preventing the device from ever suspending again;\ndisabling twice underflows the usage count and triggers a\n\"Runtime PM usage count underflow\" warning.\n\nBail out early when the requested state matches the current state.\nWhile at it, switch to pm_runtime_resume_and_get() so a failed\nresume is propagated to userspace instead of silently marking the\nevent enabled.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:07:50", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:00:24", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b2d7a97d75b648a643f60d77f4d6d70161268855", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/685d9d1e5c47e024413981fb7eddab86132b04a1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/56fe8e5f313a64e458bb6f8b982de925345e21a7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8e76ab81319858736ccf23141e9415f9a1869337", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/70b9482926ca92862460e659f5e5fde99ae0b4fa", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0fc740c25c9abb25113398ebb58e2f2ce57741a7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/470edb012b1d9a4fba1cd59e329e60f0798c791a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/579c049b4cb6fc72ce2c505fc5334540be0efcd3"], "aliases": ["GHSA-cp7w-v98j-9px9", "CVE-2026-90249"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.22, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "11fe6526-bb9c-37d8-82c9-5cdb33b6be2d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.188"}, {"id": "260d0627-04fb-34c9-b47f-c1e585613786", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.270"}, {"id": "32338559-f325-3ee2-b5a0-3166a1d90f54", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "97d642e23037c5545266f9564c9b81e6db81b122 <b2d7a97d75b648a643f60d77f4d6d70161268855"}, {"id": "326af4ad-7c15-34a4-b321-207ced232bed", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "97d642e23037c5545266f9564c9b81e6db81b122 <70b9482926ca92862460e659f5e5fde99ae0b4fa"}, {"id": "35646f3d-0431-3f02-8ebe-a24ba99425da", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "3b6135f3-7811-3827-b4dc-3254e349dd02", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "97d642e23037c5545266f9564c9b81e6db81b122 <685d9d1e5c47e024413981fb7eddab86132b04a1"}, {"id": "65474dd7-ebca-3659-825a-e503d10e68f5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "97d642e23037c5545266f9564c9b81e6db81b122 <8e76ab81319858736ccf23141e9415f9a1869337"}, {"id": "7e75b983-d460-3d87-8f3b-91a470e69216", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.7"}, {"id": "80ef40c4-9007-3c39-a656-d9ec56678e28", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "83366add-ce2a-3728-bbfc-930fca55e6df", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "97d642e23037c5545266f9564c9b81e6db81b122 <56fe8e5f313a64e458bb6f8b982de925345e21a7"}, {"id": "94d280bd-44c7-3499-86a0-89270eecf261", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "97d642e23037c5545266f9564c9b81e6db81b122 <470edb012b1d9a4fba1cd59e329e60f0798c791a"}, {"id": "9d868fa6-a608-3a33-a92f-3d34a468bb22", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.221"}, {"id": "b275b1cc-d59a-3fa5-b303-f64f25bbd9fb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "b94d05f7-e130-32ed-b2fa-088cb227567c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Lin